From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:44:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Count the monsters and players in each chunk slice

A mob hunting for a target asks for a 33x33 box every few ticks and almost always
finds nothing. Counted on a crowded world: 146 million candidate tests against
595 matches, and the class test rejected 1% of them - the slice scan is spent
proving an absence.

PaperSpigot already keeps a per-slice count of items and of inventories so a
query can skip a slice that holds none. This adds the same for IMonster and for
EntityHuman, which is what mobs actually spend their time looking for.

The player count needs nothing new: getEntitiesOfTypeWithinAAAB already picks its
count array off the requested class, and every mob hunting a player asks for
EntityHuman or a subclass. The monster count does, because the golem asks for
EntityInsentient and it is the predicate that requires IMonster - so the
predicate carries a marker, AthenaMonsterOnly, which
PathfinderGoalNearestAttackableTarget puts on the selector it composes when the
goal was built on IMonster.VISIBLE_MOB_SELECTOR or mobSelector. Both begin with
'entity instanceof IMonster' and every layer above them only narrows, so a slice
with no IMonster holds nothing the predicate would have accepted.

debugVerifyAthenaIndexes checks both counts against the slice every tick.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaIndexAudit.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaIndexAudit.java
index ef77e8ca0cec8bcbb90b82038deaa6f8802a8aa3..2f24738411531038bc991f6ae416690496a5f152 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaIndexAudit.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaIndexAudit.java
@@ -193,6 +193,32 @@ public final class AthenaIndexAudit {
             for (int slice = 0; slice < chunk.entitySlices.length; ++slice) {
                 ++bucketChecks;
                 java.util.List<Entity> flat = chunk.entitySlices[slice];
+                // Athena - the per-slice counts a target query skips whole slices on
+                int monsters = 0;
+                int humans = 0;
+
+                for (int idx = 0; idx < flat.size(); ++idx) {
+                    Entity entity = flat.get(idx);
+
+                    if (entity instanceof IMonster) {
+                        ++monsters;
+                    }
+
+                    if (entity instanceof EntityHuman) {
+                        ++humans;
+                    }
+                }
+
+                if (monsters != chunk.auditMonsterCount(slice)) {
+                    report("slice " + slice + " of chunk " + chunk.locX + "," + chunk.locZ + " holds "
+                            + monsters + " monsters but its count says " + chunk.auditMonsterCount(slice));
+                }
+
+                if (humans != chunk.auditPlayerCount(slice)) {
+                    report("slice " + slice + " of chunk " + chunk.locX + "," + chunk.locZ + " holds "
+                            + humans + " humans but its count says " + chunk.auditPlayerCount(slice));
+                }
+
                 java.util.List<Entity>[] buckets = chunk.auditBuckets(slice);
 
                 if (buckets == null) {
diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaMonsterOnly.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaMonsterOnly.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f483b56ecb75b04496a99ce7d6708d3b11974b24
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaMonsterOnly.java
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+package net.minecraft.server;
+
+// Athena - marker for a predicate that can only ever accept an IMonster.
+//
+// A mob hunting for a target asks for a 33x33 box every few ticks and almost always finds nothing:
+// measured on a crowded world, 146 million candidate tests against 595 matches. Testing each
+// candidate faster does not help that; the only thing that does is not looking at slices that
+// cannot hold a match. Chunk keeps a per-slice count of IMonster entities for exactly that, in the
+// same way PaperSpigot already counts items and inventories, and this marker is how a query says
+// the count applies to it.
+//
+// PathfinderGoalNearestAttackableTarget puts it on the selector it composes when the goal was built
+// on IMonster.VISIBLE_MOB_SELECTOR or IMonster.mobSelector. Both begin with
+// "entity instanceof IMonster", and every layer the goals wrap around them - the golem's own
+// selector, the NOT_SPECTATING conjunction - only narrows further, so a slice holding no IMonster
+// holds nothing the composed predicate would have accepted either.
+public interface AthenaMonsterOnly {}
